# Owner Creation via OfficeFloor Function Injection — Findings

This is a Spring PetClinic REST app where request handling has been converted from Spring `@RestController` to **OfficeFloor function injection**. Spring DI, security, persistence, and DTOs are unchanged; each REST endpoint is defined by a YAML pipeline of function classes. Build is **Maven** (`pom.xml`).

## 1. Owner entity/model — NO `customerCode` field

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

Owner extends `Person` (which extends `BaseEntity`). Fields: `address`, `city`, `telephone`, `email`, `registrationDate`, `pets` (from Owner) + `firstName`, `lastName` (from Person) + `id` (from BaseEntity). **There is no `customerCode` field anywhere in the model.** Key parts:

```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "owners")
public class Owner extends Person {
    @Column(name = "address") @NotEmpty private String address;
    @Column(name = "city") @NotEmpty private String city;
    @Column(name = "telephone") @NotEmpty
    @Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", message = "Phone number must be E.164, e.g. +61412345678")
    private String telephone;
    @Column(name = "email") private String email;
    @Column(name = "registration_date") private java.time.LocalDate registrationDate;
    @OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL, mappedBy = "owner", fetch = FetchType.EAGER)
    private Set<Pet> pets;
    // getters/setters; setEmail lower-cases; pet helpers; toString
}
```

Supporting classes:
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java` — `firstName`, `lastName` (both `@NotEmpty`).
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/BaseEntity.java` — `Integer id` (`@Id @GeneratedValue(IDENTITY)`), `isNew()`.

## 2. OfficeFloor YAML for POST /owners

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` — a 4-stage pipeline (note: `ValidateOwner` is NOT used here; it's used by the PUT path):

```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: checkTelephone

checkTelephone:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.CheckUniqueTelephone
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save

save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond

respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```

Related list endpoint `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.GET.yml`:
```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"
service:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ListOwners
  govern: [ readonly-transaction ]
```

Pipeline convention: functions communicate via OfficeFloor variables — a producer writes `Out<Owner> built` and downstream functions read `@Val Owner owner`. The HTTP body is bound with `@RequestBody` and Spring beans (mapper, repository) are injected as plain parameters.

## 3. POST pipeline function classes (full source)

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`

**BuildOwner.java** — validates required fields, maps DTO→entity, normalizes telephone to E.164, validates email:
```java
public class BuildOwner {
    private static final Pattern EMAIL = Pattern.compile("^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$");

    public void service(@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, Out<Owner> built)
            throws MissingOwnerFieldsException {
        Map<String, String> required = new LinkedHashMap<>();
        required.put("firstName", request.getFirstName());
        required.put("lastName", request.getLastName());
        required.put("address", request.getAddress());
        required.put("city", request.getCity());
        required.put("telephone", request.getTelephone());
        List<String> missing = required.entrySet().stream()
                .filter(e -> e.getValue() == null || e.getValue().isBlank())
                .map(Map.Entry::getKey).toList();
        if (!missing.isEmpty()) throw new MissingOwnerFieldsException(missing);
